WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.359
Partitioning by follower can keep a person’s follow
list and prepared feed together.

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:11.548
It cannot simultaneously place every followed
author’s original posts beside every reader without

00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:12.314
duplication.

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:18.694
Social relationships cross partition boundaries, so
a normalized read may fetch from several owners.

00:00:18.694 --> 00:00:25.010
The graph model makes the tension visible: balancing
vertices and keeping related vertices together

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.605
are competing objectives.

00:00:26.605 --> 00:00:32.657
A hybrid design precomputes updates for ordinary
authors and merges selected high-fan-out authors’

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:35.251
recent posts when a reader opens the feed.

00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:39.759
This avoids sending every popular post to millions
of inactive followers.

00:00:39.759 --> 00:00:45.687
The threshold is a workload decision: compare
expected fan-out cost against the reads that would

00:00:45.687 --> 00:00:50.874
need an on-demand merge, including freshness and
cache behavior for popular content.
